# secrets: never commit
.env
*.env
!.env.example

# nothing from the private vault belongs here
private/
*.pdf

# vault exports arrive in these shapes. Blocked at the extension so a diagram or a
# spreadsheet dragged in during a late-night edit cannot be added by `git add .`.
*.csv
*.xlsx
*.drawio
*.vsdx

# agent tooling. Per-machine settings record permission grants and command history,
# which is machine state rather than project state. Previously covered only by a
# machine-global ignore, so a fresh clone elsewhere would have made them committable.
#
# Written as a glob rather than the literal filename on purpose: the sanitisation
# guard's hostname pattern matches the mDNS suffix in that name and fires on it. The
# repo's rule is to rewrite the text rather than weaken the pattern, and this glob is
# that rewrite. Shared project settings (.claude/settings.json) still commit normally.
.claude/settings.*.json

.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
